# Narrative Writing Rules

When writing Learning Path narratives into narrative-master-PHASE5.md, follow these rules strictly to avoid timeouts and token waste.

## Write One Lesson at a Time

**NEVER write more than one lesson in a single Write or StrReplace call.**

A lesson = 1 Lesson Opener + 3 Chapters + 1 Lesson Ending.

### Workflow Per Lesson:
1. Write the Lesson Opener + Chapter 1 (including New Characters + Wisdom + Reflection + Journal)
2. StrReplace to append Chapter 2 (Bridge + Narrative + Wisdom + Reflection + Journal)
3. StrReplace to append Chapter 3 (Bridge + Narrative + Wisdom + Reflection + Journal) + Lesson Ending
4. Save and verify before moving to next lesson

## Chapter Structure (always use this exact format):

```
### Chapter N: [Title]

**Bridge:** (Ch2 and Ch3 only — one paragraph connecting from previous)

**Narrative:**

**Story Group 1:**
[~250 words of narrative]

**Story Group 2:**
[~250 words of narrative]

**Story Group 3:**
[~250 words of narrative]

**[Name]'s [Topic] Wisdom:**
[~200 word technical summary — always uses master's name + topic descriptor]

**New Characters:** (Ch1 only, for new masters)
**[Name]**
[2-3 sentence description + quote]

**Reflection Questions:**
- Question 1?
- Question 2?
- Question 3?

**Aria's Journal - Day [N]**
*[~200 word journal entry]*

---
```

## Content Length Targets:
- Story group: ~250 words (2-3 paragraphs)
- [Name]'s [Topic] Wisdom: ~200 words (replaces both old "Mastery" and "Wisdom" sections)
- Journal: ~200 words
- Lesson Opener: ~100 words
- Lesson Ending: ~350 words (300-400 range, 5-7 paragraphs)
- LP-boundary ending (lesson X.4): slightly longer, summarizes entire LP
- Series finale (LP15.4): 500-700+ words, references previous characters and realms

## Lesson Ending Quality Checklist:
- [ ] Master reflects on what Aria learned (1-2 paragraphs)
- [ ] Aria reflects on her growth or the lesson's significance (1-2 paragraphs)
- [ ] Binary summarizes key concepts in a display/projection (1 paragraph)
- [ ] Foreshadowing: names the next master and hints at their teaching (1 paragraph)
- [ ] Warm, narrative tone — no code examples
- [ ] 300-400 words (aim for 350)

## Wisdom Section Format (STANDARDIZED):
- All chapters use **[Name]'s [Topic] Wisdom:** format
- The [Name] is the lesson's master (short name, e.g., "Jasmine" not "Test Master Jasmine")
- The [Topic] describes what the section covers (e.g., "Testing Pyramid", "Advanced Validation")
- Ch1: Wisdom section appears after New Characters intro
- Ch2/Ch3: Wisdom section appears after Story Group 3
- There is NO separate "[Topic] Mastery" section — it has been merged into Wisdom
- There is NO plain "[Name]'s Wisdom:" without a topic — always include a topic descriptor

## Character Restrictions:
- **Debuggora the Owl** stays with Test Master Jasmine at the Testing Tower (LP8.1). She does NOT appear in any other lesson — not LP8.2, not LP8.3, not LP8.4, not LP9-15. She is Jasmine's companion only.
- No LP1-7 masters return in active teaching roles. They can only be mentioned in passing. Aria and Binary are the only constants across all LPs.
- Each new master appears in exactly 1 lesson (3 chapters) and does not return.

## Do NOT:
- Write multiple lessons in one tool call
- Write more than one chapter per StrReplace append
- Try to write all chapters of a lesson at once in one tool call
- Include Debuggora in any lesson after LP8.1
